# Administrative command settings (read by `python -m app.cli create-teacher|seed`, by the one-shot
# "cli" service of docker-compose, and by you when you run the command by hand). Copy to
# backend/.env.cli (git-ignored) and replace CHANGE_ME with the password of the CLI role, the one
# DB_CLI_PASSWORD in backend/.env.roles set when the bootstrap created the role.
# It holds only that credential: no API, worker, migrator or administrator setting. The API and the
# worker never receive this file, which is why the API cannot create teacher accounts.
# Deliberately NOT called DATABASE_URL: the command fails instead of silently using another credential.
# Host "db" is the docker compose service name; use "localhost" or "127.0.0.1:5442" from the host.
CLI_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://asistente_cli:CHANGE_ME@db:5432/asistenteia
